pref.statusLayout = Status bar items
pref.statusLayout.desc = Show/hide and reorder the items on the right of the status bar in a separate window (also from the status bar's right-click menu). C = CPU, M = memory, D = disk, N = network show the whole system; click an item for details.
pref.statusInterval = Status bar load refresh (ms)
pref.statusInterval.desc = How often CPU, memory, disk and network are read.
pref.tabStatusbar = Tab status bar
pref.tabStatusbar.desc = Shows a status bar at the bottom of each panel with the current folder's item count and Git branch.
pref.gitRefresh = Git summary refresh interval (s)
pref.gitRefresh.desc = Re-query the tab status bar's git summary (⇡⇣ + ! ? ✘ » = $) at this interval. Folder/.git watching, file operations and window focus already refresh it immediately, so this is a safety net for other cases (network drives etc.). 0 = no periodic refresh.
pref.gitEnabled = Show git summary
pref.gitEnabled.desc = Show the branch and status summary in the tab status bar. Off = git is never run.
pref.gitUntracked = Count untracked files in git summary
pref.gitUntracked.desc = Include the untracked file count (?) in the summary. Turn off if a very large repository feels slow (git status -uno).
pref.gitDiverged = Diverged marker (⇕) when both ahead and behind
pref.gitDiverged.desc = Prefix ⇡⇣ with ⇕ when the branch is both ahead of and behind its upstream.
pref.watchGitSettle = git re-query settle delay (ms)
pref.watchGitSettle.desc = After a folder or .git change, wait until things have been quiet this long before querying the git summary again. Keeps git from being launched back to back while changes keep coming (fetch, checkout, builds). 0 = immediately.
pref.watchGitTimeout = git query time limit (s)
pref.watchGitTimeout.desc = If git status runs longer than this, it is stopped and treated as a failure (a failed repository then follows the retry interval).
pref.watchGitRetry = git query failure retry interval (s)
pref.watchGitRetry.desc = A repository whose git query failed or was stopped after exceeding the time limit is not queried again until this interval has passed (even on file changes or focus return). A safeguard so very large repositories do not keep using CPU and disk. 0 = no retry until a manual refresh or toggling the git summary off and on.
pref.watchGitBackground = Keep refreshing git while the window is inactive
pref.watchGitBackground.desc = When off, the periodic git summary refresh (Status bar setting) pauses while the window is inactive or minimized. It is queried again as soon as you return to the window, so leaving this off is usually lighter.
pref.toolbarOnColor = Toolbar: toggled-on color
pref.toolbarOnColor.desc = How a toggled-on toolbar button looks. Line color = light accent background, outline and icon drawn in the color below. Accent = outline and icon follow the accent settings.
pref.toolbarOnColor.line = Line color
pref.toolbarOnColor.accent = Accent
pref.toolbarOnLineColor = Toolbar: toggled-on line color
pref.toolbarOnLineColor.desc = Outline and icon color of a toggled-on button, as #RRGGBB.
pref.toolbarIconScale = Toolbar: icon image scale (%)
pref.toolbarIconScale.desc = Size of the icon image inside each toolbar button. The button size stays the same.
